      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "The goal is reliable smaller steps, then\nuseful delegation. TextCraft checks the\nfinal inventory and quantities.\n\nThe new lead is repairing what the learner\nsees before a correct action. The results\nhere are not a test of learned recursion."
    },
    {
      "idx": 1,
      "label": "2",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "SFT means supervised fine-tuning: copy a\ndemonstrated next action. The diagram is\nsimplified.\n\nThe repair changes histories, not 366\nanswers or 23 training steps. Answer\ntokens are matched; input length and\ncomputation are not. It still uses a known\ncorrect action list."
    },
    {
      "idx": 2,
      "label": "3",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "All models get 23 training steps. Counts\nare 1 to 14, 2 to 13, and 3 to 17, out of\n32. The first two rows share goals; the\nthird adds eight.\n\nA randomized repair also helped. Neither\nclearly beat discovery. More training\npartly rescues the original teacher. These\npanels are exploratory."
    },
    {
      "idx": 3,
      "label": "4",
      "overlay": 0,
      "note": "One reward-training step per setting.\nFamiliar: 9 to 13 and 14 to 16. Different\ngoals: 4 to 5 and 5 to 5.\n\nEight different target roots, same recipe\nworld; not held-out confirmation. The raw\ngain is one attempt. Fresh-A learning and\nextra SFT remain pending. Only this slide\nadvances to 05:30 UTC."
    },
    {
      "idx": 4,
